{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\cite{SGA4}", "REF_0002": "\\cite{KS}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:130d7d05ca49863a9e8245880bc46c374ed4a885ed4c0dda43e9b8993df6eb3c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we define what a topology on a category is as\ndefined in <REF_0001>. One can develop all of the machinery of\nsheaves and topoi in this language. A modern exposition of this material\ncan be found in <REF_0002>. However, the case of most interest for algebraic\ngeometry is the topology defined by a site on its underlying category.\nThus we strongly suggest the first time reader\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0001>skip this section and all other sections of this chapter<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001>!\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d6b74ccaecaa54d7dd43abba38a1131578bcc097361c45cb1546f3848263ca61", "unit_id": "tag:00YW:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$S \\subset h_U$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-sieve}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dd5e318a01f6aca901ffc246763b8e73b58f4fe45264f1a57f502bfda83bb7f0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ae888ded0a868c3e8a1ef7d29c3e502f6628a0c5de3b39fc76ebc7d0c30dd73c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. Let <MATH_0002>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>sieve <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a subpresheaf <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d711b1aa2e7a06494894fd6f5a825f3bc6bcea6afa6a05989130f12db5fa8ab9", "unit_id": "tag:00YX:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$S(T)$", "MATH_0004": "$T \\to U$", "MATH_0005": "$S(T) \\subset h_U(T) = \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(T, U)$", "MATH_0006": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-property-sieve}\n\\left.\n\\begin{matrix}\n(\\alpha : T \\to U) \\in S(T) \\\\\ng : T' \\to T\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\} \\Rightarrow\n(\\alpha \\circ g : T' \\to U) \\in S(T')\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0007": "$S \\to h_U$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4c75771db08bc8c5a1dc164ba994d25e2284723083d258d18ae4b9372aadb51f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:768bb8b7edeef7ebef389f1e90acaf74235448abda3b259d2e5ae2e6a6924133", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words, a sieve on <MATH_0001> picks out for each object\n<MATH_0002> a subset <MATH_0003> of the set\nof all morphisms <MATH_0004>. In fact, the only condition\non the collection of subsets\n<MATH_0005>\nis the following rule\n<MATH_0006>\nA good mental picture to keep in mind is to think of the\nmap <MATH_0007> as a ``morphism from <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>''.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:82071a36b65689873992d0246a792907ce089d702a500d7c5c4c8eaa94ea2913", "unit_id": "tag:00YW:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{item-sieve-generated}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$U_i \\to U$", "MATH_0010": "$S(U_i)$", "MATH_0011": "$S = h_U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-sieves-set}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:02dea8c6b05a442e31def69800d246962fe89332a620deec8ff2522941565a29", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bfadeba9b0268b92772609cb20e03f4f854b780e43b4e7965e94b620e30fbdc6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. Let <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The collection of sieves on <MATH_0003> is a set.\n<STRUCT_0003> Inclusion defines a partial ordering on this set.\n<STRUCT_0004> Unions and intersections of sieves are sieves.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nGiven a family of morphisms <MATH_0004>\nof <MATH_0005> with target <MATH_0006>\nthere exists a unique smallest sieve <MATH_0007> on <MATH_0008> such that\neach <MATH_0009> belongs to <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0006> The sieve <MATH_0011> is the maximal sieve.\n<STRUCT_0007> The empty subpresheaf is the minimal sieve.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e1010a8cce33dcb107a242eb06a2077a98b07f73dbdade4cbfa84ee0e1ad9f9b", "unit_id": "tag:00YZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\prod_{U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})} \\mathcal{P}(\\mathcal{F}(U))$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{P}(A)$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$S \\leq S'$", "MATH_0007": "$S(T) \\subset S'(T)$", "MATH_0008": "$T \\to U$", "MATH_0009": "$S \\subset S'$", "MATH_0010": "$S_i$", "MATH_0011": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "MATH_0013": "$\\bigcup S_i$", "MATH_0014": "$(\\bigcup S_i)(T) = \\bigcup S_i(T)$", "MATH_0015": "$T \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0016": "$\\bigcap S_i$", "MATH_0017": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0018": "$h_{U_i} \\to h_U$", "MATH_0019": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-image}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0005": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0006": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0007": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0008": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:369e35b5c384bcc4d877cc023ae865e702b06ffc21f786761d3ab611e19124af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1ee5d0fcff90e9c6c260eec43287dff2a745898ada90a2b37767e334c490a037", "source_text": "By our definition of subpresheaf, the collection of\nall subpresheaves of a presheaf <MATH_0001> is a subset of\n<MATH_0002>.\nAnd this is a set. (Here <MATH_0003> denotes\nthe powerset of <MATH_0004>.) Hence the collection of sieves on <MATH_0005>\nis a set.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nThe partial ordering is defined by: <MATH_0006> if and only if\n<MATH_0007> for all <MATH_0008>. Notation: <MATH_0009>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nGiven a collection of sieves <MATH_0010>, <MATH_0011> on <MATH_0012> we can\ndefine <MATH_0013> as the sieve with values\n<MATH_0014> for all\n<MATH_0015>.\nWe define the intersection <MATH_0016> in the same way.\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nGiven <MATH_0017> as in the statement, consider\nthe morphisms of presheaves <MATH_0018>. We simply\ndefine <MATH_0019> as the union of the images (Definition <REF_0001>)\nof these maps of presheaves.\n\n<STRUCT_0007><STRUCT_0008>\nThe last two statements of the lemma are obvious.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:86ab0c869e1349f4c4ee08abde65910a8a02ccbe9a7a1b3c614b001a522bca58", "unit_id": "tag:00YZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{f_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$f_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-sieves-set}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{item-sieve-generated}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-sieve-generated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:65b03b2b3706a7ba3c49665d1e3915faf9f51e6b30f54859bbd62c7404a0b2e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a56bd305a9304e3721cfada27539350fa0ea5632f97caf200d05e161084cd3e6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nGiven a family of morphisms <MATH_0002>\nof <MATH_0003> with target <MATH_0004> we say the sieve\n<MATH_0005> on <MATH_0006> described in Lemma <REF_0001>\npart (<REF_0002>) is the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>sieve  on <MATH_0007>\ngenerated by the morphisms <MATH_0008><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:54daca9cc27a62070ba7fbd38caeb0dc52bd45f9acfe4fa221dea1c057dce35c", "unit_id": "tag:00Z1:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$S \\subset h_U$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$S \\times_U V$", "MATH_0008": "$V$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n(\\alpha : T \\to V) \\in (S \\times_U V)(T)\n\\Leftrightarrow\n(f \\circ \\alpha : T \\to U) \\in S(T)\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-pullback-sieve}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:112856a633696ba593ee53e74b11304d6a25cb18970faaf4e56b3085bdbd1b34", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:79d2ba90aadaadc75da28690e575d1c9407ba59f0983cd6e76b4a9a22d0e1783", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sieve. We define the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>pullback of <MATH_0005> by <MATH_0006><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> to be the sieve\n<MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008> defined by the rule\n<MATH_0009>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:edc5d5b9c27bac73cdb0871d98829b34ef774f4a02deaf1cabdb9f589ab4f844", "unit_id": "tag:00Z2:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S \\times_U V$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f : V \\to U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-property-sieve}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:809491bcc325895ab47f4e6192eddca8004d78a9636f481cea053fd3ee1f6e90", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d093b3f3b8dde9f2569bd0e50874f59e1b99dc0546594d08a53150901559d1f6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe leave it to the reader to see that this is indeed a sieve\n(hint: use Equation <REF_0001>).\nWe also sometimes call <MATH_0001> the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>base change<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof <MATH_0002> by <MATH_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:94e981f7d8190aff195b713f88abfccfb20361041d83d96de422d50252a154d0", "unit_id": "tag:00YW:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$S \\times_U V = h_V$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-sieve-section}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:35e5d58f29f9bd06fba9a51bae5d4fbdc326164ffdb52d53e64288b5d5581aff", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f11dbdfb7dcb54a8bea2d15abb8707d76122b8409625755ff14509475b7dd91a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nLet <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a sieve on <MATH_0004>.\nIf <MATH_0005> is in <MATH_0006>, then\n<MATH_0007> is maximal.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d0cbf79f40c4790b4dcc5dc0bd652c91a7bd9e9daec195dab3f499525ae799f2", "unit_id": "tag:00Z3:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:24bf8ffaeb30e10d726207913786f3c9728701a9a08123e887d9d580e9c8581e", "source_text": "Trivial from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:47070d6d7e3b0dbe96205569b2965bfefc2f0233b5b41d0cab7488886faf9ac0", "unit_id": "tag:00Z3:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$J(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$S \\in J(U)$", "MATH_0009": "$S \\times_U V$", "MATH_0010": "$J(V)$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$S'$", "MATH_0013": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0014": "$S \\in J(U)$", "MATH_0015": "$f \\in S(V)$", "MATH_0016": "$S' \\times_U V$", "MATH_0017": "$J(V)$", "MATH_0018": "$S'$", "MATH_0019": "$J(U)$", "MATH_0020": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0021": "$S = h_U$", "MATH_0022": "$J(U)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-topology}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3b21ac650650f982f8b4363a3800a48ccc934146233bba8c19b0e7ecd0c9842a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:beadb5cd1662551b2c4eba167e2e02aacd5fd057bfdcccc7e17b59a7b7f35a2e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>topology on <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is given\nby a rule which assigns to every <MATH_0003>\na subset <MATH_0004> of the set of all sieves on <MATH_0005> satisfying\nthe following conditions\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> For every morphism <MATH_0006> in <MATH_0007>, and\nevery element <MATH_0008> the pullback <MATH_0009>\nis an element of <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012> are sieves on <MATH_0013>,\nif <MATH_0014>, and if for all <MATH_0015> the pullback\n<MATH_0016> belongs to <MATH_0017>, then <MATH_0018> belongs to <MATH_0019>.\n<STRUCT_0004> For every <MATH_0020> the\nmaximal sieve <MATH_0021> belongs to <MATH_0022>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95588315735e736cd2ea04d35fcff58091774d4c5807797c7290c046a516de71", "unit_id": "tag:00Z4:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00YW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$J(U)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09b665e3d59c2c36ee107d0a8f46b7df264666ac110bf82dfcfeb81d52a92d27", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3f4b7431531e63ca1e67163c16096fc0419d4ecaf22e44a48db71ea005917ea5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this case, the sieves belonging to <MATH_0001> are called\nthe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>covering sieves<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d8f6ac16ccf7131b3b797c2a793de8e9f9971571a6f5ba96b1215dd52de8c8cc", "unit_id": "tag:00YW:prose-0004"}
